-- InfyQ HRMS -- large-scale enterprise demo dataset
-- =====================================================================
-- Generated for the "Infyq" schema (backend/db/hrms.txt). ADDITIVE ONLY:
-- creates one brand-new company ("InfyQ", code INFYQ) and populates it
-- end-to-end. Does NOT delete, modify, truncate, rename, or touch any
-- existing table, column, constraint, row, or role belonging to any other
-- company already in this database.
--
-- Guarded (safe to run even if these already exist from prior seeding):
--   core_currencies (INR, by code) and core_permissions (global catalog,
--   by code) use INSERT ... SELECT ... WHERE NOT EXISTS.
-- NOT idempotent / not guarded (assumes a single run against a fresh
-- target that has never had an "InfyQ" company before): the company row
-- itself and every row scoped under its company_id (roles, org structure,
-- 150 employees, attendance, leave, payroll, performance, recruitment,
-- documents, assets, training, travel/expense, and 14 demo login users).
-- Re-running this whole script a second time would create a SECOND
-- "InfyQ" company's worth of duplicate data (core_companies.code is
-- UNIQUE, so the company insert itself would fail loudly first -- that
-- is the intended safety net against an accidental double-run).
--
-- Demo login users (password for all: Welcome@123), one per built-in role,
-- so every RBAC role can be exercised end-to-end in the running app.
--
-- No schema changes were required -- every table/column referenced below
-- already exists in backend/db/hrms.txt.
-- =====================================================================

